cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Explainability is Encodability: A Sheaf-Theoretic Foundation for Neural Network Interpretability"
abstract: >-
  A network is interpretable iff its layer family can be generated by a single
  source object along the layer ladder. This turns "black box" into a positive
  proposition: a black box is a network with no code. Formalized in Lean 4 with
  zero sorry, no classical logic, entirely over the rationals.
